%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 612 612
%%Title: Moss Goes to the Sea, page 13: inside her shell
/Seed where { pop } { /Seed 14 def } ifelse  Seed srand
(lib/cb_book.ps) run
cb-ground
250 cb-night [0.30 0.32 0.56] cb-sky-wash
250 cb-sea cb-sea-paint
-9 600 222 30 [0.75 0.85 0.95] 1.1 cb-waves
300 415 9 131 cb-stars
newpath -9 -9 moveto -9 190 lineto 200 200 420 170 621 180 curveto 621 -9 lineto closepath cb-sand 0.85 cb-wash
newpath -9 -9 moveto -9 190 lineto 200 200 420 170 621 180 curveto 621 -9 lineto closepath cb-dusk 0.07 cb-bigwash
/cb-tuck true def
306 120 80 cb-moss
% the song, curling out of the shell
[1 2 3] { /i exch def
  newpath 310 206 i 26 mul 70 add 50 i 6 mul sub 130 i 6 mul add arc
  cb-moon cb-rgb << /Width 2.4 /Taper 0.8 /Waver 0.4 >> pkliner } forall
cb-paper cb-rgb
(Then she curled up inside her shell, the way snails do. And there, in her own small house, she could still hear the sea singing:) 60 584 492 /center cb-text pop
cb-fontit findfont 30 scalefont setfont (hush . . . hush . . . hush.) 306 448 showctr
13 cb-folio
showpage
